"""ARCH-48 — Real-Time Collaborative Review & Live Presence.
One atomic, idempotent apply for the whole milestone (backend, console, verifiers, ingress, docs).

Run from backend/:

    python apply_arch48.py --check      # report every file, write nothing
    python apply_arch48.py              # apply
    python apply_arch48.py              # again: every line reads "already applied"
    python apply_arch48.py --rollback   # restore what the last apply replaced
    python apply_arch48.py --list       # the files this script owns

Accepted starting point: 7680b0c ("ARCH-47 DONE"), with or without the two
handoff prompts ARCH-47's apply writes (ARCH-47-HANDOFF-PROMPT.md and
ARCH-48-HANDOFF-PROMPT.md were never committed; the ARCH-48 prompt as the
project stores it is accepted too and replaced by the canonical text). Every
file is brought to this package's result. A file already carrying a later
milestone's sentinel (ARCH49-S1: and on) is reported as superseded.
Line endings and a UTF-8 byte-order mark (deploy/Caddyfile) are kept as
found (an LF and a CRLF checkout both apply; the sha256 is taken over LF
text). New files are written LF, as .gitattributes pins.

ARCH48-S1:apply. GENERATED from `git diff 7680b0c` plus the new files
(24 new, 42 edited through 143 anchors); the generator refuses to emit if any file carries no ARCH48-S
sentinel (ARCH-47's two handoff prompts excepted), and every edit is an
anchor that occurs exactly once when it applies, checked against the final
sha256.
"""

